134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Since its inception in 2022, the Youth Tech Asia Challenge \(YTAC\) has become a premier platform for young tech enthusiasts across Asia to showcase their innovation and problem-solving skills. The competition brings together students with a passion for technology and aims to inspire the next generation of tech leaders. Over the years, YTAC has grown from a local event to an international platform, providing a space where students can demonstrate their creativity, technical skills, and collaboration abilities. In year 2025, a dynamic and innovative programming competition - Tech-Hackathon added designed to inspire and challenge young minds in the fields of technology and software development. Aimed at students and young enthusiasts, the hackathon provides a platform for participants to tackle real-world problems through coding, collaboration, and creativity. By combining teamwork with individual skill development, the hackathon encourages participants to think critically and develop practical solutions to everyday technical challenges.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
